> Too often in the early game I overuse my bow and run out of arrows.

Combat strategy changes as the game progresses.  Early on I
quiver daggers even for a class that ends up archer.  I'm playing
samurai lately and I've been enhancing dagger to basic very early
in the game then eventually switching to bow.  And by the mazes
of Gehennom melee power is critical.  It's a tough lesson to figure
out when to use what type of combat.

Later in the game blessed arrows and high luck they stop
disappearing,.  Until you start encountering disenchanters and rust
monsters and the occasional combat close to water.  There's
always some way for arrows to dissappear ...

The good thing about arrows is once it becomes easy to bless a
stack of them enough have built up from traps, centaurs, orcs
and elves that they are a plentiful resource from there on in the
game.  But before that, daggers continue to rule even for archer
classes.


